name conceptnet-relations
# ConceptNet's page "Relations in ConceptNet 5": a table, a row for each relation, under the headings the page gives:
#   | Relation URI | Description | Examples
#   | /r/IsA | A is a subtype or a specific instance of B; every A is a B. ... | car → vehicle; Chicago → city
# A relation's URI, /r/IsA, is ConceptNet's address for the relation IsA: the relation is its name. The page is read
# as the text it is.
match Relations.md

tier line by \n

# Both lines are unresolved obligations (Laplace-Engine#32): "Description" and "Examples" are the table's column
# headings, never a relation. The description is the relation's gloss, [IsA, its description as the page words it],
# which needs a line that gives a relation in the documentation's words ("line PATTERN :: relation TEXT"); the engine
# has none, and a bare pair [IsA, the description] would say it under no meaning at all. The examples (car → vehicle)
# are edges the relation joins, content records of the relation, not something said of it under a heading.
line ^\| */r/([^ |]+) *\| *([^|]*[^| ]) *\| :: predicate Description
line ^\| */r/([^ |]+) *\|[^|]*\| *([^|]*[^| ]) *$ :: predicate Examples
